<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Titus Labienus</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 100–45 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/1st-century-bce">1st century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Titus Labienus was a Roman general, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/julius-caesar">Julius Caesar</a>'s most trusted legate in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gallic-wars">Gallic Wars</a> of 58–50 BCE. He defeated the Treveri in 53 BCE and the Parisii and their allies near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lutetia">Lutetia</a> in 52 BCE. In the civil war he joined <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pompey">Pompey</a> against Caesar and was killed at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-munda">Battle of Munda</a> in 45 BCE.</p></div>
